{
  "text": " Hi everyone, Louisa asked me to create this quick video note just to let you all know that I am still alive. I'm currently in Europe, I'll be back in the United States this weekend. And I have been working periodically on my substack. My most recent article is about the death rates that we got from the Social Security death master file. And it showed a huge 60% increase and the peak was in September of 2021. And at first I said, what doesn't make any sense, right? Because the peak of vaccination in the United States was in April. How could this happen five months later? And so I got to thinking about it and I realized that some of our assumptions that we had assumed were correct, were actually not correct. So it turns out that a lot of people do in fact die within 24 hours of vaccination and a lot of people die within two weeks and three weeks and four weeks of vaccination. But what's really astonishing is that the peak of the deaths is actually five months later. And so it was no surprise then that when you looked at this data, which is 18 to 55 year olds in the Social Security master death file, which is not publicly available by the way. So had I have a whistleblower inside HHS, provide that data to me. And when I saw it, at first it didn't make sense to me, but now it does. And that data is correct. And it basically shows that the death peaks five months later. So people who've had relatives that died five months after their last dose, now you actually have statistical evidence showing that that's the most probable time for someone to die after the vaccine. Now they could die a year after they got their last dose. And I know people who have been vaccinated who then succumbed a year later, or you could die within 24 hours. So the window of opportunity for death actually extends out from basically T0 to about a year after with the peak being five months later. And what was astonishing is that after I published this, one of my readers pointed out that just three weeks earlier he used the European data, not the US data at all. He used the European data and he found exactly the same five month delay using a completely different data set. So what this means is that like when we look at the Canadian deaths, I looked at Canadian deaths again and the number of Canadian deaths of young doctors 50 and under were 15 in 2021, yet there were only six in 2020. So that's an increase in factor of 2.5 times more deaths. That would be hard to explain. Something else can have an effect size like that. But now we have a way to say yes, these doctors didn't die right after the vaccine. They died throughout the year. And I have to look to see where those deaths were centered, but I'll bet they were centered somewhere around the September timeframe. So I'm going to have to go back and look at that. But that's the big result for today. The other thing is that I was swimming in a pool and I was noticing that my heart rate increased while I was swimming. And the interesting thing is that Canadian doctors are dying when they're running and they're swimming. So when they're doing physical activity. And when you put this together with some of the results that Jessica Rose had on her sub-stack about the blood clots and so forth, I think possibly what may be happening here is that the physical exertion is actually perhaps moving these blood clots, these massive, and they're not blood clots, they're clots. They're these rubbery clots. But what might be happening is that through physical exertion, you're kind of moving this clot that might have been stretched out and kind of compressing it and twisting it around so that it blocks the blood from flowing through your blood vessels. And so this may in fact be the cause of heart attacks and strokes that happen. And what you would explain, because how else could you explain why a doctor, a young doctor would die, multiple doctors have died while swimming. I mean, that's not something you normally drown. Like if you're a doctor, you don't drown when you're swimming, you're not going to swim. So it's really, really unusual. But the fact that athletes are dying at hugely increased rates and people who are doing sports, running, swimming, whatever, this blood clot combined with the extra pressure and moving clots around, I think maybe possibly explaining that as well. So hope that's a quick update and I will see you all next Thursday. Bye.",
